    "knowledge_point": "Multiplying Complex Matrices",
    "problem": "If $\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}-3+5\\text{i} & 4-3\\text{i} \\\\ -4\\text{i} & 5-5\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}-3\\text{i} \\\\ 4-5\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]\\,$, then $\\,Ax=$",
    "worked_solution": "Multiplying the matrix by the vector using the usual method, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =[\\begin{aligned}-3+5\\text{i} & 4-3\\text{i} \\\\ -4\\text{i} & 5-5\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-3\\text{i} \\\\ 4-5\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}(-3+5\\text{i})(-3\\text{i})+(4-3\\text{i})(4-5\\text{i}) \\\\ (-4\\text{i})(-3\\text{i})+(5-5\\text{i})(4-5\\text{i})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}(15+9\\text{i})+(1-32\\text{i}) \\\\ (-12)+(-5-45\\text{i})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}16-23\\text{i} \\\\ -17-45\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
